'''Kyūshi Kasei''' (九紫火星) is one of the {{ill|Nine Stars|ja|九星|12=draft|12=draft|12=draft}} used in {{ill|calendars|ja|暦|12=draft|12=draft|12=draft}} and {{ill|fortune-telling|ja|占い|12=draft|12=draft|12=draft}}. In the Post-Heaven Lo Shu Square, it occupies the southern position.
Among the Nine Stars, it is the only one associated with the Fire element in the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|12=draft|12=draft|12=draft}}.
In the daily cycle of the Nine Stars, the day closest to the {{ill|summer solstice|ja|夏至|12=draft|12=draft|12=draft}} that falls on a Kanoto (甲子) day is designated as Kyūshi, marking the transition from Yang to Yin. At that time, the last day of the previous Yang cycle and the first day of the new Yin cycle both belong to Kyūshi, making it appear for two consecutive days.
